Package: nestedANOSIM
Title: Hierarchical (Nested) ANOSIM and Graphics for Community Data
Version: 0.0-3
Authors@R:
    person("Francisco Enrique", "Fontúrbel", , "fonturbel@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8585-2816"))
Description: Extends the one-way analysis of similarities (ANOSIM) in
    'vegan' to a hierarchical design in which a nested factor is evaluated
    within each level of a main factor. In a single call it runs ANOSIM on
    the combined factor, on the main factor, and on the nested factor within
    each main-factor level (with optional multiple-testing correction), and
    summarises sample size, richness and abundance per group. A companion
    similarity percentages (SIMPER) analysis with the same design reports
    which taxa drive each difference, as tidy tables. Also provides
    'ggplot2' graphics for ANOSIM rank dissimilarities and for non-metric
    multidimensional scaling (nMDS) ordinations with convex hulls for any
    number of groups. Includes a camera-trap dataset of mistletoe visitors
    from Las Chinchillas National Reserve, Chile.
